  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mohammad Jakeer Hussain Mohd. Jakeer vs The State Of Telanana on 13 June, 2025 Author: N.Tukaramji Bench: N.Tukaramji The Honourable Sri Justice N.Tukaramji Criminal Petition No. 6974 Of 2025 Order",
    "facts": "This Criminal Petition is filed under Section 528 of Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 (for short 'BNSS, 2023') seeking quashment of the proceedings , against the petitioner in Crime No.151 of 2025 of Narsampet Police Station, Warangal District. 2. The petitioner is sole accused in Crime No.151 of 2025 registered for the offences punishable under Sections 272 and 275 of Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 (for short 'BNS, 2023'). 3. Accordingly, the complainant and his staff apprehended the petitioner and seized tobacco products viz., 1) 40 Amber packets, worth of Rs. 40 x 1500 = 60,000/-, 2) JK 3320 packets, worth of Rs.40 x 875 =35000 and 3) 160- Anaz Tobacco Mohammad Jakeer Hussain Mohd. Jakeer vs The State Of Telanana on 13 June, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/113219867/ 1 Packets, worth of Rs.100 x200 = 20000, which were total worth of Rs.1,15,000/- under cover of panchanama. Thereafter, the Director General of Police, Telangana State issued Circular Memorandum in RC.No. 295/R1-NS/2022 with directions to the Station House Officers not to interfere with the business activities, who carry out the business as per rules of Food Safety and Standards Authority of India and also not to take any coercive measures against the tobacco traders as long as the order of the Hon'ble Supreme Court is in force.",
    "arguments": "4. The prosecution case in brief is that the petitioner/accused is involved in selling and purchasing the banned Tobacco products and the Police concerned seized the said Tobacco products worth of Rs.1,15,000/-. 5. Learned counsel for the petitioner would submit that the Coordinate Bench of this Court vide Criminal Petition Nos.3731 and Batch [LEAKAGE_MASK] the proceedings against the petitioners therein by 2 NTR,J passing common order dated 27.08.2018. He further submits that the 2nd respondent has registered the present crime in violation of the orders passed by this Court. Hence, prayed for quashment of the proceedings against the petitioner in the crime. 6. Learned Additional Public Prosecutor would submit that the petitioner has to face either investigation or trial and prove his innocence and instead of doing so, he has filed the present criminal petition, which cannot be considered at this stage. 7. 10. Having regard to this factual position, a Coordinate Bench of this Court in Crl.P.No.6235 of 2022 held that against the allegations of illegal selling and transportation of tobacco products the Sections 188, 269, 270, 272, 273, 278, 328 read with Sections 511, 336, 409 and 420 of I.P.C., would not attract and [LEAKAGE_MASK] the proceedings against the petitioners therein.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "4. The prosecution case in brief is that the petitioner/accused is involved in selling and purchasing the banned Tobacco products and the Police concerned seized the said Tobacco products worth of Rs.1,15,000/-. 5. Learned counsel for the petitioner would submit that the Coordinate Bench of this Court vide Criminal Petition Nos.3731 and Batch [LEAKAGE_MASK] the proceedings against the petitioners therein by 2 NTR,J passing common order dated 27.08.2018.",
    "respondent_arguments": "He further submits that the 2nd respondent has registered the present crime in violation of the orders passed by this Court. Hence, prayed for quashment of the proceedings against the petitioner in the crime. 6. Learned Additional Public Prosecutor would submit that the petitioner has to face either investigation or trial and prove his innocence and instead of doing so, he has filed the present criminal petition, which cannot be considered at this stage. 7.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "10. Having regard to this factual position, a Coordinate Bench of this Court in Crl.P.No.6235 of 2022 held that against the allegations of illegal selling and transportation of tobacco products the Sections 188, 269, 270, 272, 273, 278, 328 read with Sections 511, 336, 409 and 420 of I.P.C., would not attract and [LEAKAGE_MASK] the proceedings against the petitioners therein."
  },
